//? Title: Painter overdraw: stable object depths
//? Subtitle: Canonical C++ producers, original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A single depth key orders each complete rectangle; larger depths paint first.
Inclusive bounds are clipped to the raster. Equal-depth objects retain input
order, so the later object wins overlaps. This is a constant-depth rectangle
demonstration: interpenetrating surfaces and cyclic polygon visibility require
another representation. No external dataset is needed.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and scope

A single depth key orders each complete rectangle; larger depths paint first.
Inclusive bounds are clipped to the raster. Equal-depth objects retain input
order, so the later object wins overlaps. This is a constant-depth rectangle
demonstration: interpenetrating surfaces and cyclic polygon visibility require
another representation. No external dataset is needed.

For a covered pixel, its final owner minimises the pair(depth,-input_index); the
second component implements the documented equal-depth tie. Constant object
depth is the restricted model, not a general polygon visibility solution.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native diagram use the same producing run. Captured records own
their values; the report does not reconstruct the algorithm.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/painters_algorithm_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <iostream>
#include <sstream>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <numeric>
#include <vector>
#include <string>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/painters_algorithm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t =
        dm::algorithms::painter_trace({{0, 0, 1, 0, 3, 1}, {1, 0, 2, 0, 1, 2}},
                                      3, 1);
    std::print("| object | pixel | before | after |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &r : t.writes)
        std::print("| {} | ({},{}) | {} | {} |\n", r.object, r.x, r.y, r.before,
                   r.after);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0}, std::format("Actual order\n{}", t.order));
    d.node("n1", {8, 0}, std::format("Actual assignments\n{}", t.writes.size()));
    d.node("n2", {16, 0}, std::format("Final pixel ids\n{}", t.raster[0]));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/painters_algorithm_tiny.svg");
}
```
