> API and interpretation

All four blocks are complete editable C++ programs. Numerical tables retain raw
native values; figures display only those returned records. Trace limits count
documented logical records or scalar entries, not peak bytes or wall-clock work.
Validation is complete before unchecked indexing; captured histories are
educational owned storage. A returned result is interpreted under the
algorithm-specific scope above, without a universal optimality, convergence or
statistical-quality claim.

[MIT visibility notes|https://groups.csail.mit.edu/graphics/classes/6.838/S98/meetings/m23/painters.html]
explain back-to-front drawing and why cycles require splitting; the native
rectangle model is deliberately narrower.

> Verification

This ten-report batch passes 89 CTest cases, 20 ASan/UBSan cases with all ten
producing families directly instrumented, 62 compiled and executed public
examples, 200/200 scoped file definitions plus 15/15 exact PCG class
definitions, and ten representative clangd hovers. Independent Python
hashlib/HMAC and arbitrary-integer PCG checks verify 75189 records with 123243
checks. Native independent per-pixel visibility, exhaustive prefix reversals,
quadratic LIS, integer perceptron updates, sampled-label tail counts and
exhaustive Boolean-cover checks supplement frozen valid-input comparisons for
all ten producers. Ten checkout and ten byte-identical installed development
headers compile independently; an installed-header native consumer links and
runs. All 40 complete programs execute; all 40 native figures have been visually
reviewed. HTML/Markdown exports preserve computed result rows and identical
image bytes. These are scoped native checks. Receipts:
`build/mepml-conversion/batch-274-283/`.
